    "body": "Problem:\r\nComputing window geometry before redraw synchronously parses and restarts highlight queries for each unchecked line. This repeats work after every edit when a query uses conceal_lines, even in plain Markdown.\r\n\r\nSolution:\r\nCheck a window-height of buffer lines per conceal callback, capped at EOF. Reuse the existing checked-row cache and its edit/tree invalidation. Rescan the requested row after providers run so that marks added for later rows cannot conceal preceding text. Preserve cursor, window and namespace conceal rules, and the normal redraw highlight state.\r\n\r\nCover parse batching, cache reuse, edits, insertion and deletion with injected fenced-code concealment. A 17-line plain Markdown buffer needs one synchronous conceal parse instead of sixteen.\r\n\r\nAI-assisted",
    "closed_at": null,
    "comment_data": [],
    "comment_regular_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Benchmark, please (and real-world use cases, not (just) academic micro-tests).\r\n\r\nAnd tests are not free; consider whether a 250 line spec is really needed for this. (LLMs tend to believe so, but they are mostly wrong.)",
